The treaty facts are taken from the United Nations Treaty Collection (https://treaties.un.org/), retrieved 30 October 2026:
treaty names, kinds of action and dates only. The Treaty Collection's robots.txt (Crawl-delay: 2) was obeyed.

The catalogue-gazette facts (Lao titles, numbers, dates, responsible bodies) come from the list of all current laws published by the Lao Official Gazette, https://laoofficialgazette.gov.la/, retrieved 30 October 2026; no law text is copied. The catalogue and wipo-treaties facts come from WIPO Lex, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/, whose content is published under CC BY 4.0 (https://www.wipo.int/web/terms-of-use); only facts are copied. Source: World Intellectual Property Organization. Changes made by Lexifina: records were turned into one Markdown file per record, with the dates arranged as a git history. WIPO does not endorse this repository.

The legal-system facts are from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org/), released under CC0 1.0 Universal.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
